  "schoolyard_use_notes": "This towering tree has thick, reddish-brown bark that can be used to discuss bark texture and fire resistance. Its needle-like leaves are evergreen and arranged in flat sprays, providing a year-round example of photosynthesis. The tree produces small, woody cones that can be used to illustrate seed dispersal and growth cycles. Its impressive height and longevity make it ideal for lessons on forest ecosystems and the importance of conservation.",
